{"_id":"68a736428ec3d8323af20295","nodeId":"qefnsugcveizVq2TORRgn","roadmapSlug":"typescript","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:45.916Z","description":"# Combining Types\n\nCombining types in TypeScript allows you to create new, more complex types from existing ones. This is achieved through features like unions and intersections. A union type lets a variable hold values of different types, while an intersection type combines multiple types into a single type that has all the properties of each individual type. These mechanisms provide flexibility and expressiveness when defining the shape of your data.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Union Types in TypeScript","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html#union-types","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243971"},{"type":"article","title":"Intersection Types in TypeScript","url":"https://www.typescripttutorial.net/typescript-tutorial/typescript-intersection-types/","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243972"},{"type":"article","title":"Type Aliases","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html#type-aliases","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243973"},{"type":"article","title":"Keyof Type Operator","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/keyof-types.html#handbook-content","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243974"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T11:14:56.641Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041649f","title":"Scrimba - Learn TypeScript","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"https://v2.scrimba.com/learn-typescript-c03c?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/typescript/content/qefnsugcveizVq2TORRgn.md"}